# AWS Load Balancer Infrastructure Setup

This repository contains the architecture design and deployment configuration for an high-availability AWS network infrastructure using both an **Application Load Balancer (ALB)** and a **Network Load Balancer (NLB)**.

---

## 📐 Architecture Diagram

```mermaid
graph TD
    Client[Internet Traffic]

    subgraph VPC [VPC: vpc-0c4d7d44e0d930cce]
        ALB[test-alb: Application Load Balancer]
        NLB[test-NLB: Network Load Balancer]
        
        subgraph Subnet [AZ: us-east-1a]
            EC2_1[mywebserver-1-ALB / t3.micro]
            EC2_2[mywebserver2-ALB / t3.micro]
        end
    end

    Client -->|HTTP / Layer 7| ALB
    Client -->|TCP / Layer 4| NLB
    ALB -->|Target Group| EC2_1
    ALB -->|Target Group| EC2_2
    NLB -->|Target Group| EC2_1
